Requires:
- macOS 10.15 (Catalina) through macOS 15+ (Sequoia)
  Supported on both Apple Silicon (M1/M2/M3/M4) and Intel (x86_64) Macs
- rar binary in PATH if RAR packaging is used (optional, ZIP is the default)

Notifications:
- Native macOS Notification Center banner notifications work out-of-the-box
  via built-in AppleScript (`display notification`) without external dependencies.
- Optional: "terminal-notifier" is also supported if installed via Homebrew.

Install - Client:
1. Copy `ulf` binary to your PATH:
   - On Intel Macs: `sudo cp ulf /usr/local/bin/ulf && sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/ulf`
   - On Apple Silicon: `sudo cp ulf /opt/homebrew/bin/ulf && sudo chmod +x /opt/homebrew/bin/ulf`
   - Or for single user (no sudo): `mkdir -p ~/.local/bin && cp ulf ~/.local/bin/ulf && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/ulf`
2. Edit `ulf` and configure your server details in the server config section.
3. Test upload manually via terminal (e.g. `ulf -i /path/to/test.txt`).

Install - Workflow / Quick Actions (Finder Integration):
1. Copy all workflow packages to `~/Library/Services/`:
   `cp -R Workflows/*.workflow ~/Library/Services/`
2. Open each workflow at least once in Automator to register it with macOS.
3. In Finder, right-click on any file or folder -> check the "Quick Actions" menu.
4. (Optional) Assign Keyboard Shortcuts:
   - Open System Settings -> Keyboard -> Keyboard Shortcuts -> Services (or Quick Actions)
   - Locate the upload and screenshot actions and set your preferred shortcuts (e.g. Cmd+Alt+1, Cmd+Alt+2).

macOS Permissions (System Settings -> Privacy & Security):
- Screen Recording:
  Required for `Screenshot.workflow` so `screencapture` can record your screen/selection.
  Go to System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Screen & System Audio Recording (or Screen Recording)
  and ensure Automator / Finder / Terminal has permission.
- Files and Folders / Full Disk Access:
  If uploading files from protected folders (~/Desktop, ~/Documents, ~/Downloads),
  ensure Finder / Automator has file access permissions when prompted.

Install - Server:
- Webserver: Any HTTP/HTTPS server (nginx, caddy, apache). Upload directory e.g. `/var/www/`
- SSH: Non-root user with permissions to write and chmod uploaded files.
- HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2, and HTTP/3 are all fully supported for upload verification.
